306C 173402 092606 N13:11.02 W090:00.45 Here we attempted a new dispersed aggregation protocol.  Three passes (strips) were made through
307C 174402 092606 N13:11.60 W090:01.65 the aggregation, with each 25X observer tallying the number of dolphins seen on each side of the
307C 174402 092606 N13:11.60 W090:01.65 trackline, without reporting angle and distance for each dolphins or small groups of dolphins.
307C 174402 092606 N13:11.60 W090:01.65 The idea is that each transect will provide an estimate of density, assuming an appropriate ESW,
307C 174402 092606 N13:11.60 W090:01.65 and the 3 passes in different directions provide the size and shape of the aggregation.
307C 174402 092606 N13:11.60 W090:01.65 The comments noting start and end of each pass give the positions at the edge of the "school".
